-- This sql codes for DATA VALIDATION of raw data to make sure data is ready to used and clean

## 1. Data Quality & Pre-Analysis Validation

### 1. Business Purpose & Strategy
Before running exploratory data analysis (EDA) or feature engineering, raw data must pass strict quality and sanity checks. 
This script audits raw dataset for primary key uniqueness, boundary violations, domain range constraints, and unexpected NULL values. 

Conducting data validation upfront ensures that downstream CSAT scores, customer segmentation, and geographical drivers are calculated on clean, reliable telemetry.

### Data Audit Checklist SQL query & Findings

  ## Uniqueness & Primary Keys** | `Customer_ID` | Verify there are no duplicate record IDs. | Distinct row count vs. total row count audit
  
     Select count(distinct *)
     From workspace.default.customer_satisfication_dataset

  ## Filtering for non-standard categorical group than A,B,C ##

    Select *
    From workspace.default.customer_satisfication_dataset
    Where group not in ('A', 'B', 'C')

## Check is there any satisfication store less than 1 or more than 10 or empty ##

    Select *
    From workspace.default.customer_satisfication_dataset
    Where Satisfaction_Score < 1 or Satisfaction_Score > 10 or Satisfaction_Score is null

## Check if the age is null or less than 0 or more than 100 ##

    Select *
    From workspace.default.customer_satisfication_dataset
    Where age is null or age > 100 or age <0

## Check type of loyalty level ##

    Select distinct Loyalty_Level
    From workspace.default.customer_satisfication_dataset

## Check different type of satisfication factor
    
    Select distinct Satisfaction_Factor
    From workspace.default.customer_satisfication_dataset
    
